COUNCIL OF ELROND: FULL TRANSCRIPT (abridged, somehow)
Recorded by the House of Elrond, Rivendell

ELROND: We are gathered to decide one thing. Let us not decide eleven.
GLOIN: A messenger came to Erebor. He asked after hobbits, and offered rings.
BOROMIR: I had a dream. My brother had it too. Nobody else? Nobody?
GANDALF: It is the One Ring. I checked. There was fire, and writing.
LEGOLAS: About Gollum. We may have lost him. He climbed a tree.
GANDALF: You lost him.
LEGOLAS: He climbed a very tall tree.

ERESTOR: Could we give it to Bombadil?
GANDALF: He would take it if we asked, and forget it by supper.
GLORFINDEL: Then cast it into the sea.
ELROND: The sea is deep, but not deep enough, and not forever.
BOROMIR: Why not use it? Against him?
EVERYONE: No.
BOROMIR: I was only asking.

ELROND: Then it must go to the fire where it was made.
(Silence. A long one. Someone coughs. Bilbo offers to go; nobody accepts.)
FRODO: I will take the Ring, though I do not know the way.
SAM (from under a window): Not alone you won't!
ELROND: Nobody invited you.
SAM: No, sir.

ACTION ITEMS
  1. Nine walkers to be chosen. (Done, see who-carries-the-ring.md.)
  2. Scouts to be sent out. (Done; they found nothing, which was worrying.)
  3. Shards of Narsil to be reforged. (Assigned: the smiths.)
  4. Bilbo to stop telling the troll story. (Not done.)

Next meeting: none planned. Everyone hopes it went well.
